title: Example scene
set-bg: example_background.png
new-page: trueeeeee # this should flag an error (it does not)
on-arrival: {!
  console.log("Arrived at example scene");
  asfasf; //this should flag an error (it does not)
  if (true) { 
    console.log("This is valid JS code");
  }
  Q.yes = true;
  iff () { // this should DEFINITELY flag an error (it does not)
  }
  if (Q.yes = 1) { // this should flag an error (it does not)
    Q.result = "yes";
  } else if (Q.no == true) {
    Q.result = "no";
  }
!}

Where do you want to go?

[? if yes = 1 or no = 1 : some extra text ?]

# backkkk is valid, even if it does not have ": something" after. In that case, the scene title will be displayed
- @backkkk
- @scene_a: Here
- @scene_b: There
- @1800a: To 1800 # this raises an error (it reads the scene name as "1800" rather tahn "1800a")
- @non_existing_sceneeeeeee: This should raise an error! (it does not!)
- #tag_example
- #tag_unexample

# tag_unexample should raise an error, as no scene in the directory has that tag (it does not)

